description.narrative:
Output: Existing water supply systems improved in seven towns. Indicator: Groundwater sources, reservoirs and/or pumping stations in at least five of the participating PWWs developed and/or rehabilitated. Achievement: Y Progress/Status: Achieved. Physical works in 5 PWWs completed and operational since 31 August 2022. Data Source: Project progress and project completion reports;
Baseline and follow-up surveys in project towns;
Construction records and evaluation reports, including GAP 6-monthly reports and midterm review. Actual value: Y

Output: Existing water supply systems improved in seven towns. Indicator: Provision made for approx. 2,000 new household connections in at least two of the participating PWWs, with equal access for all households and connections for the poor subsidized up to 100%. Achievement: 1500 Progress/Status: Achieved. Approx 9,392 sets of household connection provided to 5 PWWs. Data Source: Project progress and project completion reports;
Baseline and follow-up surveys in project towns;
Construction records and evaluation reports, including GAP 6-monthly reports and midterm review.

Output: Existing water supply systems improved in seven towns. Indicator: Water laboratories and analytical equipment provided in at least four of the participating PWWs. Achievement: Y Progress/Status: Achieved. 5 towns provided with laboratory equipment.
Data Source: Project progress and project completion reports;
Baseline and follow-up surveys in project towns;
Construction records and evaluation reports, including GAP 6-monthly reports and midterm review. Actual value: Y

Output: Existing water supply systems improved in seven towns. Indicator: Water treatment plants in at least six of the participating PWWs (re-) constructed, improved and/or rehabilitated. Achievement: 4 Progress/Status: Achieved. Physical works in 6 PWWs completed and operational. Data Source: Project progress and project completion reports;
Baseline and follow-up surveys in project towns;
Construction records and evaluation reports, including GAP 6-monthly reports and midterm review.

Output: New water supply system provided for Stung Treng Indicator: Provision made for approximately 4,600 new household connections, with equal access to all households and connections for the poor subsidized up to 100%. Achievement: N Progress/Status: Achieved. Installed 4,600 new household connections and continued increasing for 7000 house service connection provisions Data Source: Project progress and project completion reports;
Baseline and follow-up surveys in project towns;
Construction records and evaluation reports, including GAP 6-monthly reports and midterm review. Actual value: N

Output: Project implementation supported and O&M developed Indicator: The EA, IA, PMU, and PIUs develop at least one gender-sensitive and inclusive policy governing water resource management or service delivery. Achievement: N Progress/Status: Achieved. Gender Awareness Training and the refresher on GAP Orientation to the officials and the staffs have been conducted to PMUs/PIUs for 29 times, 252 people, 130 females (51.59%). Data Source: Project progress and project completion reports;
Training records and evaluation of capacity development programs;
Organization&apos;s employment records and annual reports;
Construction records and evaluation reports, including GAP 6-monthly reports and midterm review. Actual value: N

